# Juno Hale, Bram's apprentice. Full depth (docs/narrative/BIBLE_WAVE2.md section 2). Fast, run-on, delighted; exaggeration with a
# self-deflating tail; craft vocabulary; the labels. Sentences up to 24 words, one exclamation mark a line at most, never "whatever".
# Teases Bram affectionately, never criticizes his work. Cozy only. Works 9 to 6 at the forge, closed Mondays.

addto npc.juno.talk

# ---- seasons ----
0 season:spring => juno.spring.1 cat=seasonal :: Okay, okay, okay: spring means hinges. Every gate in Wetherell decided to fall off in the same week!
0 season:spring => juno.spring.2 cat=seasonal :: Plow blades, hoe heads, a bucket with a hole I labeled "Bucket (Hole)". It's been a very busy thaw.
0 season:spring => juno.spring.3 cat=seasonal tag=funny :: The first warm day, Bram opened the forge door and said "Hm." That's the longest spring speech I've ever heard.
0 season:spring => juno.spring.4 cat=seasonal :: New iron smells like rain in a drawer. I know that's not a smell. It is, though!
0 season:spring => juno.spring.5 cat=seasonal :: My birthday's in spring. I'm not saying a word. I've labeled the date in the calendar. In red. Twice.
0 season:spring => juno.spring.6 cat=seasonal rarity=uncommon :: Every spring I forge one thing I don't sell. This year it's a tiny, perfect spoon. Don't ask.
0 season:summer => juno.summer.1 cat=seasonal :: The forge in summer is a sauna with opinions. I've stopped wearing sleeves. Bram's pretending not to see.
0 season:summer => juno.summer.2 cat=seasonal tag=funny :: I keep a bucket of water by the door. Wren called it "the swimming pool". I put a sign on it. It says so.
0 season:summer => juno.summer.3 cat=seasonal :: Long evenings, short tempers, perfect weather for a clasp. I've made forty. I regret none!
0 season:summer => juno.summer.4 cat=seasonal :: Piper and I swam off the beach after closing. She sang. I hammered. The fish left.
0 season:summer => juno.summer.5 cat=seasonal :: Sunburn on one arm only, from the forge door. I look like a half-cooked loaf. A proud one.
0 season:summer => juno.summer.6 cat=seasonal rarity=uncommon :: The summer festival's coming, and I've entered a medal in the "made by hand" table. It's mostly polish. And nerves.
0 season:fall => juno.fall.1 cat=seasonal :: Fall: scythes, axes and a small flood of gift commissions. Everyone suddenly loves someone with a belt buckle.
0 season:fall => juno.fall.2 cat=seasonal :: The forge is the best seat in the village now. Bram says it isn't. Bram sits in it daily.
0 season:fall => juno.fall.3 cat=seasonal tag=funny :: I labeled the leaves on the forge roof. "Leaf (Hissing)". They hiss when they land. I'm delighted.
0 season:fall => juno.fall.4 cat=seasonal :: Bram's birthday's in fall. He thinks nobody knows. I've made a card. It's mostly diagrams.
0 season:fall => juno.fall.5 cat=seasonal :: Cold mornings make iron feel honest. You can hear every dent. I love it. I also love tea.
0 season:fall => juno.fall.6 cat=seasonal rarity=uncommon :: Harvest week, I walk to the beach and talk to the tide about metal. It nods. Sort of.
0 season:winter => juno.winter.1 cat=seasonal :: Winter at the forge: the warmest room in Wetherell. Half the village comes in to "ask about nails".
0 season:winter => juno.winter.2 cat=seasonal :: Snow on the roof, sparks in the air, tea in a tin cup. I could weep. I might. It's soot.
0 season:winter => juno.winter.3 cat=seasonal tag=wholesome :: Winter evenings, Bram tells me one thing about his old teacher. One thing. I've been counting. I've got eleven.
0 season:winter => juno.winter.4 cat=seasonal :: Frost on the anvil! It melts in a heartbeat. I labeled it "Anvil (Sulking)".
0 season:winter => juno.winter.5 cat=seasonal :: Long nights are good for filing. And for thinking about what to make that's never been made.
0 season:winter => juno.winter.6 cat=seasonal rarity=uncommon :: Last winter I made a snowflake in copper. It melted nothing and impressed everyone. Bram nodded. Nodded!

# ---- weekdays ----
0 weekday:mon => juno.mon.1 cat=weekday :: Monday. Bram and I are shut, and I still came in. I'm only here to label things. It's a hobby.
0 weekday:mon => juno.mon.2 cat=weekday :: It's our day off. I spent it sharpening spoons for fun. Don't judge.
0 weekday:tue => juno.tue.1 cat=weekday :: Tuesday. Wren's saloon is shut, so everyone's at the forge, warming up and asking questions.
0 weekday:tue => juno.tue.2 cat=weekday :: Slow Tuesday, good for fine work. Tiny hinges, tiny hooks, tiny sighs.
0 weekday:wed => juno.wed.1 cat=weekday :: Wednesday. Marcus is closed, so Bram's gone to sit on a bench. In silence. With him. It's adorable.
0 weekday:wed => juno.wed.2 cat=weekday :: Midweek, which means orders. Orders mean noise. Noise means I'm happy.
0 weekday:thu => juno.thu.1 cat=weekday :: Thursday. Felix is out of hooks, so I'm making some. Between us, they're lovelier than his.
0 weekday:thu => juno.thu.2 cat=weekday :: Thursdays I sharpen everything, including the bucket. Bram's looking at me. I'm sharpening the bucket.
0 weekday:fri => juno.fri.1 cat=weekday :: Friday! Everyone needs their tool done by Saturday. I've labeled the pile "Panic (Polite)".
0 weekday:fri => juno.fri.2 cat=weekday :: Friday. Orders, noise and Wren's gossip floating in through the door like a very nosy breeze.
0 weekday:sat => juno.sat.1 cat=weekday :: Saturday, market day. I'm selling clasps in the square, and Bram's in the forge saying "Hm" to a kettle.
0 weekday:sat => juno.sat.2 cat=weekday :: Saturday afternoon, my favorite hour: the forge cools, the square's loud, and nobody needs me.
0 weekday:sun => juno.sun.1 cat=weekday :: Sunday. I'm fixing things nobody asked me to fix. It's like Bram, but louder.
0 weekday:sun => juno.sun.2 cat=weekday :: A quiet Sunday, and a very small anvil, and a very big idea I'm not telling you.

# ---- weather ----
0 weather:sunny => juno.sunny.1 cat=weather :: Perfect weather. The forge is a furnace, the street is a postcard, and I'm a sweaty, grinning idiot.
0 weather:sunny => juno.sunny.2 cat=weather :: Sun on the anvil, sun on the roof, sun on my nose. I'm freckled in three places. New record.
0 weather:sunny => juno.sunny.3 cat=weather :: Bright day. I opened both doors. Bram closed one. We're negotiating.
1 weather:rain => juno.rain.2 cat=weather :: Rain on the roof of the forge: the best sound in the world, and I'll fight anyone who says the sea.
1 weather:rain => juno.rain.3 cat=weather tag=funny :: Everybody brought in their tools to dry. Bram's running a laundry. I've labeled the line "Damp (Dignified)".
1 weather:rain => juno.rain.4 cat=weather :: Rain makes the hot iron hiss like a cat that's been insulted. I love that cat. I'm that cat.
1 weather:storm => juno.storm.1 cat=weather :: Thunder! The anvil rings back. They're old friends. I think they're arguing.
1 weather:storm => juno.storm.2 cat=weather :: Storm night, and I'm filing a clasp by lantern light. It's romantic, if you squint and love clasps.
1 weather:storm => juno.storm.3 cat=weather :: Lightning's loud. The forge is louder. I told the sky it can try harder.
1 weather:snow => juno.snow.1 cat=weather :: Snow on the sill, glow in the forge. It looks like a postcard with a very hot secret.
1 weather:snow => juno.snow.2 cat=weather :: Everything's muffled. Even my hammer. It feels like working inside a very large pillow.
1 weather:snow => juno.snow.3 cat=weather tag=wholesome :: Snow day. Bram opened the door a crack so we could watch it fall. He didn't say why. I knew.
1 weather:wind => juno.wind.1 cat=weather :: Windy, so the door's arguing with the draft. The draft's winning. I've labeled it "Rude".
1 weather:wind => juno.wind.2 cat=weather :: The ash is going everywhere. I'm gray to the elbows. I look like a very tired ghost.
1 weather:wind => juno.wind.3 cat=weather :: Blustery day. The forge roars, the roof rattles, and I've lost my hat. Again. It's a pattern.

# ---- time of day ----
0 hour<10 => juno.morning.1 cat=time :: Early! The fire's still sleepy. I'm coaxing it. Don't talk too loud. It startles.
0 hour<10 => juno.morning.2 cat=time :: First heat of the day, first good idea. I wrote the idea on my glove. It's already smudged.
0 hour<10 => juno.morning.3 cat=time :: Before the shop opens it's just me, the iron and a very philosophical kettle.
0 hour>=10 && hour<16 => juno.midday.1 cat=time :: Midday! Peak heat, peak noise, peak "Hm" from Bram. I've never been happier or sweatier.
0 hour>=10 && hour<16 => juno.midday.2 cat=time :: Busy. Don't stand in the sparks. They have terrible manners.
0 hour>=10 && hour<16 => juno.midday.3 cat=time :: Afternoon's when the best iron gets made. I have no proof. It's just a feeling in my elbows.
0 hour>=16 && hour<20 => juno.evening.1 cat=time :: Closing soon. The fire's low, the floor's a disaster, and I'm still making one more clasp.
0 hour>=16 && hour<20 => juno.evening.2 cat=time :: Evening. I sweep, Bram sits, and the forge hums like a sleepy cat. It's my favorite part.
0 hour>=16 && hour<20 => juno.evening.3 cat=time :: Last job of the day is always the hard one. It's like the universe is checking my attendance.
0 hour>=20 => juno.late.1 cat=time :: Late! The anvil's still warm, and so am I. I'm not working. I'm "letting the metal talk".
0 hour>=20 => juno.late.2 cat=time :: Past closing. I should sleep. The iron says otherwise. The iron's a terrible roommate.
0 hour>=20 => juno.late.3 cat=time :: Quiet hours at the forge. Best hours. That's when I try the thing I haven't made yet.
0 map:Blacksmith => juno.here.1 cat=place :: Don't touch the one labeled "Hot". Or the one labeled "Hotter". Or the one labeled "Hm".
0 map:Blacksmith => juno.here.2 cat=place tag=funny :: Every tool has a label. Some of them are insults. Bram's chair says "Do Not". He sits anyway.
0 map:Blacksmith => juno.here.3 cat=place :: Careful, the floor has opinions. I've labeled the opinionated tile "Mister Trip".

# ---- friends (3 to 5 hearts) ----
0 hearts:juno>=3 && hearts:juno<6 => juno.fr.1 cat=tier :: Oh! You came! Okay, okay, okay, look at this clasp. It closes. First try. Don't tell Bram I cried.
0 hearts:juno>=3 && hearts:juno<6 => juno.fr.2 cat=tier :: You ask good questions. Bram never asks. He nods, and the nod has footnotes.
0 hearts:juno>=3 && hearts:juno<6 => juno.fr.3 cat=tier tag=funny :: I've labeled your spot at the forge "Guest (Welcome)". Bram crossed out the "Guest". I haven't asked why.
0 hearts:juno>=3 && hearts:juno<6 => juno.fr.4 cat=tier :: Piper says I talk to you more than I talk to the anvil. I told her that was not a comparison.
0 hearts:juno>=3 && hearts:juno<6 => juno.fr.5 cat=tier :: Look at this hinge! I made it with my own hands, a lot of tears and a little spite.
0 hearts:juno>=3 && hearts:juno<6 => juno.fr.6 cat=tier :: Tilda put a clasp on the slate in your name. That's how you know you've arrived.
0 hearts:juno>=3 && hearts:juno<6 => juno.fr.7 cat=tier tag=wholesome :: You listen to me talk about metal. Nobody listens. You take notes with your face.
0 hearts:juno>=3 && hearts:juno<6 => juno.fr.8 cat=tier :: Come by tomorrow? I might have a surprise. Or a spoon. Possibly both.

# ---- close friends (6 to 8 hearts) ----
0 hearts:juno>=6 && hearts:juno<9 => juno.cl.1 cat=tier :: I was thinking about leaving Wetherell once. Then you walked in with a muddy hat and asked about hinges. So.
0 hearts:juno>=6 && hearts:juno<9 => juno.cl.2 cat=tier tag=wholesome :: Bram's proud of me. He's never said it. I can tell by how loudly he doesn't say it.
0 hearts:juno>=6 && hearts:juno<9 => juno.cl.3 cat=tier :: You're the first person I've shown my sketches to. They're mostly doodles of clasps. And you.
0 hearts:juno>=6 && hearts:juno<9 => juno.cl.4 cat=tier :: The forge feels warmer when you're in it. Bram says it's the fire. Bram is wrong, politely.
0 hearts:juno>=6 && hearts:juno<9 => juno.cl.5 cat=tier tag=funny :: I told Wren you're my favorite customer. Now the whole village knows. Wren has been told. Wren has been told.
0 hearts:juno>=6 && hearts:juno<9 => juno.cl.6 cat=tier :: Okay, okay, okay, I made you something. It's not finished. It might never be. It's the best thing I've ever not finished.
0 hearts:juno>=6 && hearts:juno<9 => juno.cl.7 cat=tier :: You make me braver. I'm still terrified. But a bit more upright.
0 hearts:juno>=6 && hearts:juno<9 => juno.cl.8 cat=tier :: Your tools are the best looked-after in the valley. Bram says so too, and he never says anything.

# ---- confidant (9 and 10 hearts) ----
0 hearts:juno>=9 => juno.co.1 cat=tier tag=wholesome :: You're the reason I stayed in Wetherell. I should've said it years ago. Okay. I've said it. Stop looking at me.
0 hearts:juno>=9 => juno.co.2 cat=tier :: I've made a lot of clasps. The one I'm proudest of is the one I haven't made yet. It's for you.
0 hearts:juno>=9 => juno.co.3 cat=tier :: The forge is the warmest room in the world, and you've made it warmer. That's not a metaphor. I measured.
0 hearts:juno>=9 => juno.co.4 cat=tier tag=funny :: If I wrote you a letter it would be forty pages and have footnotes on soot. I'd send it, though.
0 hearts:juno>=9 => juno.co.5 cat=tier :: I used to dream of leaving. Now I dream of the next order, and you walking in.
0 hearts:juno>=9 => juno.co.6 cat=tier :: Thank you, [player]. For everything. That's the whole speech. I practiced it for an hour. It was longer.
0 hearts:juno>=9 => juno.co.7 cat=tier :: I labeled you something. It's on the back of the anvil. You can look. It says "Home."
0 hearts:juno>=9 => juno.co.8 cat=tier tag=wholesome :: Anything I make next, you'll have been there for it. That's the real signature on every piece.

# ---- moods ----
1 mood:juno=lonely => juno.lonely.1 cat=mood :: Quiet in the forge. I talk to the anvil. The anvil hasn't answered. It's rude, but consistent.
1 mood:juno=lonely => juno.lonely.2 cat=mood :: You were gone a while. I made a clasp for each day. It's a very large pile.
1 mood:juno=tired => juno.tired.1 cat=mood :: Long day. My arms are noodles. Hot noodles. With opinions.
1 mood:juno=tired => juno.tired.2 cat=mood :: A bit tired. Don't tell Bram. He'll say "Hm," and it'll be worse.
1 mood:juno=delighted => juno.delighted.1 cat=mood expr=happy :: Best day ever! I made a clasp that closes with a click. A click! I've named it "Click".
1 mood:juno=delighted => juno.delighted.2 cat=mood expr=happy emote=sparkle :: Everything worked. Everything. Even the bucket, which I'd given up on. Today is a good day!
1 mood:juno=mischievous => juno.mischief.1 cat=mood expr=happy :: I put a rubber chicken on Bram's anvil. Wren swore it was an accident. It was not an accident.
1 mood:juno=mischievous => juno.mischief.2 cat=mood expr=happy :: I labeled the kettle "Bram's Best Friend". It's been staring at him all morning.
1 mood:juno=worried => juno.worried.1 cat=mood expr=sad :: I'm worried about the piece I'm working on. I labeled it "Don't Look." Now I can't stop.

# ---- the world and the farm ----
0 farm:crops>=5 => juno.farm.1 cat=reactive :: Your field's coming along! Your hoe will need me soon. They always do. It's the law.
0 farm:crops>=5 => juno.farm.2 cat=reactive tag=funny :: So many plants! So many tools to break. I'm thrilled. Bram's quietly counting the orders.
0 farm:animals>=1 => juno.farm.3 cat=reactive :: Animals! You'll need fence hooks and a very good bucket. I know where to find both.
0 farm:animals>=1 => juno.farm.4 cat=reactive :: A cow on your farm, and a bell on the cow? I'll make you a bell. A good one.
2 festival.in:<=3 && festival.in:>0 => juno.fest.1 cat=reactive :: Festival soon! I've polished a medal and my nerves. Both shine. Neither is for sale.
2 festival.in:<=3 && festival.in:>0 => juno.fest.2 cat=reactive tag=wholesome :: Festival week. Bram's coming. Bram! In a clean shirt! I've told nobody. I'm vibrating.
2 festival.in:==0 => juno.fest.3 cat=reactive :: Festival day! The forge is shut, the square's loud, and I'm eating three things at once. Come find me!
2 birthday.in:juno<=3 && birthday.in:juno>0 => juno.bday.1 cat=reactive :: My birthday's close. I'm not hinting. I put a sign on the anvil. It says "Hint."
2 birthday.in:juno<=3 && birthday.in:juno>0 => juno.bday.2 cat=reactive :: Three days to go. Don't tell Bram. He knows. He's pretended not to for years. I love it.
3 birthday.in:juno==0 => juno.bday.3 cat=reactive expr=embarrassed emote=sweat :: It's today! Somebody told. I know who. Everyone. Everyone told. I'm very warm.
2 birthday.in:bram<=2 && birthday.in:bram>=0 => juno.bday.4 cat=reactive :: Bram's birthday! I made him a tool. He'll say "Hm." I'll cry. It's tradition.
2 birthday.in:piper<=2 && birthday.in:piper>=0 => juno.bday.5 cat=reactive :: Piper's birthday! I'm making her a fiddle bow clip. She'll haggle with me about the shine. Of course she will.

# ---- rarities ----
0 ~ => juno.rare.1 cat=rare rarity=rare tag=funny :: Technically it's art. Technically it's also a doorstop. The two are not in conflict.
0 ~ => juno.rare.2 cat=rare rarity=rare tag=funny :: I once labeled a puddle "Puddle (Ambitious)". It got deeper out of pride.
0 ~ => juno.rare.3 cat=rare rarity=rare tag=wholesome :: The first thing Bram ever taught me was patience. The second was where the good tea is hidden.
0 hearts:juno>=5 => juno.rare.4 cat=rare rarity=legendary tag=surprise emote=sparkle sfx=signature :: Don't tell Bram. (She lifts a tiny gold spoon.) I made this, with no help. Look at the mark. It's yours now.

# ---- gifts ----
say npc.juno.gift.item.resource.goldbar juno: A gold bar! Oh, oh, oh. Too soft for work, too pretty to ignore. I'm framing it. Don't tell Bram.
say npc.juno.gift.item.forage.truffle juno: A truffle! Bram loves these. I love these. We're both going to pretend I found it.
say npc.juno.gift.item.crop.pepper juno: A pepper! Hot like the forge, and twice as sensible. I'll eat it at the anvil and cry happily.
say npc.juno.gift.item.resource.copperbar juno: Copper! Clean and warm. I'll make you something with it. Don't ask what. I don't know yet.
say npc.juno.gift.item.crop.potato juno: A potato. Honest and round. It'll go on the anvil for luck, and then in my lunch.
say npc.juno.gift.item.resource.coal juno: Coal! For the forge. A very practical present. I'm a little moved. It's the soot.
say npc.juno.gift.item.crop.kale juno: Kale. Hm, as Bram says. I'll give it to the cat. The cat will give it to the floor.
say npc.juno.gift.item.forage.dandelion juno: A dandelion. I'm making a wish and I'm not telling. It's about spoons.
say npc.juno.gift.item.crop.cucumber juno: A cucumber. Cold and green and far from the forge. I'll put it in the bucket. It's been very brave.
say npc.juno.gift.cat.Fish juno: A fish! Felix's department. I'll walk it over, and take a long, tragic look at the sea on the way.
say npc.juno.gift.item.resource.ironbar juno: Iron! Bram's favorite, so mine too. I'll make a hinge so good the door will blush.
say npc.juno.gift.item.resource.stone juno: A rock! A really good one. I've labeled it "Rock (Excellent)". It goes on the windowsill.
say npc.juno.gift.item.resource.wood juno: Wood! For the fire. Marcus would weep. Bram would nod. I'll do a bit of both.
say npc.juno.gift.item.resource.bone juno: A bone. I'll make it a handle. Or a very small, serious flute. I haven't decided.
say npc.juno.gift.item.resource.slime juno: Slime. It's looking at me. ...I'll label it "Do Not Touch" and apologize to it later.
say npc.juno.gift.item.product.egg juno: An egg! Fragile and optimistic. I'll look after it. Probably.
say npc.juno.gift.item.artisan.wine juno: Wine! For the forge's anniversary. I'll share it with Bram. He'll say "Hm" and mean it.
say npc.juno.gift.item.crop.pumpkin juno: A pumpkin! I'll carve a hammer on it. A very large, very orange hammer.
say npc.juno.gift.item.food.salad juno: Salad! A respectable lunch. I'll eat it standing up, near the anvil, quickly, like a professional.
say npc.juno.gift.item.artisan.jam juno: Jam! Sticky, sweet and perfect on bread. I'll hide it from Bram. He'll find it. He always does.
say npc.juno.gift.repeat juno: Another one! You're spoiling me. I've labeled the first one "Precious" and the second "Also Precious."
